ommit the pawn structure prematurely\n- Follows classical opening principles\n\nReason: N: g8-f6 is the strongest move. It develops a piece to an excellent central square, controls important squares (e4, d5), and prepares for kingside castling. This follows sound opening principles of rapid piece development and controlling the center. The knight on f6 is also flexible and can later support d5 or e4 pawn breaks.\n\nAnswer: N: g8-f6"}
