ite.\n\nReason: Playing B: f8-b4 gives check, forcing White's king to move (since there are no pieces that can block on c3, d2, or e3 effectively). This disrupts White's development, prevents kingside castling, and develops my bishop to an active square attacking White's position. After White responds to the check, I can continue with normal development while White's king safety is compromised.\n\nAnswer: B: f8-b4"}
